// [2026-10-05 01:55 +02:00] Inventory existing exported and local data-model shapes and replace the umbrella model task with one Questions task per potential model; then remove obsolete feature-status text from the top toolbar.
// [2026-10-05 01:55 +02:00] Hide the feature status marker and task metadata from the top toolbar display while preserving the raw API entry and refresh behavior.
// [2026-10-05 02:03 +02:00] Add Questions as a valid feature status, migrate matching Questions tasks from DEVENVOPDEV.md into .features with preserved IDs, and remove the duplicate task entries.
// [2026-10-05 02:07 +02:00] Add a development-only GET /git/diff endpoint returning the unified diff from HEAD, including staged, unstaged, and untracked changes, with focused public API tests and error handling.
// [2026-10-05 02:19 +02:00] Split unresolved feature JSON-model field decisions into individual Questions features based on the existing category, urgency, commit-state, and completion-version requests; complete the parent inventory task without changing the feature storage implementation.
// [2026-10-05 02:24 +02:00] Review the repository's client/server architecture, runtime boundaries, and data-flow using project manifests and core entry points; add only evidence-backed improvement tasks to DEVENVOPDEV.md and .features.
// [2026-10-05 02:27 +02:00] Verify current system health by running the production client build, complete client and server Jest suites, and aggregate coverage workflow; record concrete results as a feature for confirmation.
// [2026-10-05 02:31 +02:00] Create shared model exports under projects/shared/src/lib/models and consume the shared API response models from client and server while retaining compatibility re-exports.
// [2026-10-05 02:32 +02:00] Organize feature records into status-focused tabs while keeping the existing search, refresh, status editing, start, completion, and edit interactions available in their respective views.
// [2026-10-05 02:36 +02:00] Remove the outer scrollbar from the feature page after moving Open, In progress, and Done lists into accessible feature-list tabs; preserve internal list scrolling where needed.
// [2026-10-05 02:44 +02:00] Add an abort action for active features that removes the item from active work, persists it back to .features with status Aborted, and keeps errors visible if persistence fails.
// [2026-10-05 02:49 +02:00] The category request names client and server as possible values but does not specify the full category set or whether category is required; keep the feature in Questions until those decisions are defined.
// [2026-10-05 02:51 +02:00] The request to create a feature describing the Open tab is already represented in .features, but does not say whether to document the existing table fields or change the UI; move it to Questions until the desired output and location are specified.
// [2026-10-05 02:53 +02:00] The uncommitted-content request does not specify its display location or how full contents should treat deleted, binary, and renamed files; keep it in Questions rather than choosing behavior.
// [2026-10-05 02:55 +02:00] Client-side priority editing is already implemented for open feature rows; numeric scores remain undefined without a scale or mapping for High, Medium, and Low.
// [2026-10-05 02:56 +02:00] The Kanban request does not define board columns or whether feature cards should be movable; keep it in Questions until lane and interaction behavior are specified.
// [2026-10-05 03:00 +02:00] Add Denied as a persisted feature status, expose it in the client status selectors, and use the existing non-active status behavior to clear the task marker and active work.
// [2026-10-05 03:04 +02:00] The duplicate-prevention request does not define the comparison rule or the user-visible response; move it to Questions rather than imposing an arbitrary duplicate policy.
// [2026-10-05 03:06 +02:00] Consolidate exact duplicate feature, Git, test-run, and filesystem response/domain types into shared model modules; preserve existing import surfaces with type re-exports and validate shared, PPT, client, and server consumers.
// [2026-10-05 03:15 +02:00] Preserve HTTP failures from BackendService file load/save/folder methods; display failures in the file editor and browser, then verify server-backed error paths and 100% client coverage.
// [2026-10-05 03:18 +02:00] Replace the stale Angular CLI/Karma template docs with the repository's npm start, dev:server, explicit Angular project builds, and Jest test/coverage workflows; document the current server build limitation.
// [2026-10-05 03:30 +02:00] Extract the navigation/current-task toolbar and bottom status toolbar into standalone components while keeping commit, polling, and service ownership in AppComponent; preserve the existing public UI and test behavior.
// [2026-10-05 03:33 +02:00] Reassess the feature-category task against the current implementation and supplied clarification; if the permitted category values remain unspecified, record the exact unresolved question and move it to Questions.
// [2026-10-05 03:35 +02:00] Reassess similar-feature merging against the creation flow; if no reliable and unambiguous similarity rule can be derived from the clarification, record the missing matching rule and move the task to Questions rather than inventing a threshold.
// [2026-10-05 03:37 +02:00] Record the supplied feature-priority score mapping as the resolved design decision: scores 1–3 map to High, 4–7 to Medium, and 8–9 to Low; close the clarification task without changing production behavior.
